---
description: After any change to code — run the BDD suite, then update the tests around what changed
alwaysApply: true
---

# Run BDD after every change

```bash
go test -count=1 ./tests/bdd/...
```

If it fails, **report the conflict** instead of adapting the test to the new behaviour: name
the scenario, the violated expectation, and offer the choice between fixing the code and
updating the test.

# Then extend the tests

- new behaviour in `core/` → a scenario in `tests/bdd/features/` plus unit tests;
- changed invariants → update the fuzz tests in `core/trading`;
- changed output format → `make test-golden-update`;
- changed contract, pages or assets → extend `api/rest/v1/spec_test.go` or
  `internal/ui/web/pages_test.go`.

Every test file carries a doc-comment saying why those tests exist and which mistake they
catch. Feature files (`# language: ru`) carry Russian comments on each `Правило:` block
explaining the business idea. Failure messages state the consequence, not just the mismatch.

# Pitfalls

- `go test ./internal/ui/...` can hang — tests under `internal/ui/daemon` reach the network.
  Run the packages you need instead.
- `go vet ./...` reports pre-existing `unreachable code` in
  `internal/ui/daemon/candlesticks_consumer/app.go`.

Full reasoning and the BDD-to-package mapping: `.ai/conventions.md`.
